###  http://example.org/exp_aa002-aldehyde-bare
<http://example.org/exp_aa002-aldehyde-bare> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                      <http://purl.org/gc/MolecularComputation> ,
                                                      <http://purl.org/gc/VibrationalAnalysis> ;
                                             <http://purl.org/dc/terms/relation> <https://doi.org/10.1021/ja00249a034> ;
                                             <http://purl.org/gc/hasResult> <http://example.org/energies_aa002-aldehyde-bare> ,
                                                                            <http://example.org/spectrum_aa002-aldehyde-bare> ;
                                             <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#generated> <http://example.org/file_aa002-aldehyde-bare_dat> ,
                                                                                   <http://example.org/file_aa002-aldehyde-bare_log> ;
                                             <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#used> <http://example.org/file_aa002-aldehyde-bare_inp> ;
                                             <http://purl.org/gc/hasBasisSet> "6-21G+(d,p)" ;
                                             <http://purl.org/gc/hasMethod> "wB97X-D" ;
                                             <http://example.org/hasHssend> "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                             <http://example.org/hasRuntyp> "OPTIMIZE" ;
                                             <http://example.org/hasSolvationModel> "PCM" ;
                                             <http://example.org/hasSolvent> "water" ;
                                             rdfs:label "Vibrational analysis aa002-aldehyde-bare" ;
                                             <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote> "geometry+frequency optimization of BARE acetaldehyde (7 atoms, NZVAR=15) at wB97X-D/6-21G+(d,p)/PCM(water), extracted from aa001h by removing both spectator waters; part of the standalone hydration thermodynamic cycle dG_hyd = G(hydrate) - [G(aldehyde) + G(water)], built to compare directly against the experimental K_h from Sorensen & Jencks (JACS 1987, 109, 4675): K_h = 1.2 +/- 0.1 at 25C, i.e. dG_exp = -0.11 kcal/mol (54.5% hydrate)" .


